WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:13.694
Vinnie and Mandy were in the attic putting old books into boxes.

2
00:00:13.695 --> 00:00:17.466
Their father popped his head in the door.

3
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:21.456
"How's it going?" he asked cheerfully.

4
00:00:21.457 --> 00:00:26.133
He stepped into the room and began to measure a wall.

5
00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:30.186
"Dad, what are you doing?" asked Vinnie.

6
00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:32.560
"Just planning some changes,"

7
00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:36.546
he replied, writing in a notebook.

8
00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:41.397
"Changes?" Mandy asked, worried.

9
00:00:41.398 --> 00:00:46.841
"The attic is going to become my new den," said Dad.

10
00:00:46.842 --> 00:00:52.383
"Your den? Why?" the children cried.

11
00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:58.421
"Oh, I just need a little space to myself," he explained.

12
00:00:58.422 --> 00:01:03.981
"Can't you use the basement?" said Vinnie, a bit rudely.

13
00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:07.972
"It's too damp down there," Dad said.

14
00:01:07.973 --> 00:01:09.848
"What's wrong with the attic?

15
00:01:09.849 --> 00:01:13.319
You're not hiding something up here, are you?"

16
00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.681
"Of course not, Dad," laughed Mandy.

17
00:01:18.682 --> 00:01:22.269
Dad put his notebook in his pocket.

18
00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:27.600
"Once you clear this space out, I'll start moving in," he said.

19
00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:31.881
He went downstairs, whistling happily.

20
00:01:31.882 --> 00:01:36.509
"What are we going to do?" asked Mandy.

21
00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.581
"We still have some time," said Vinnie.

22
00:01:40.582 --> 00:01:43.981
"But let's not waste another moment."

23
00:01:43.982 --> 00:01:47.349
He went and got the photo album.

24
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.928
"Look, Mandy," he said.

25
00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:58.307
In the picture, the old man was standing in front of a large elm tree by a building.

26
00:01:58.308 --> 00:02:03.497
Something was sticking out of its branches on a long pole.

27
00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:07.386
It was glowing.

28
00:02:07.387 --> 00:02:11.873
"What do you think this is?" asked Mandy.

29
00:02:11.874 --> 00:02:14.305
"We're about to find out!"

30
00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:17.311
said Vinnie, closing his eyes.

31
00:02:17.312 --> 00:02:22.364
The children fell down the dark tunnel.

32
00:02:22.365 --> 00:02:25.632
"Ow!" cried Vinnie.

33
00:02:25.633 --> 00:02:29.410
"Oh!" yelled Mandy.

34
00:02:29.411 --> 00:02:32.828
Vinnie landed on a damp surface.

35
00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:35.675
Mandy landed nearby.

36
00:02:35.676 --> 00:02:38.698
The air smelled of the ocean.

37
00:02:38.699 --> 00:02:42.127
They were on a long, wide pier.

38
00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:47.122
"Are you okay?" Vinnie asked, opening his eyes.

39
00:02:47.123 --> 00:02:50.601
"Yes," Mandy answered.

40
00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:55.103
She sat up and looked around, rubbing her arm.

41
00:02:55.104 --> 00:02:58.468
The pier was in the harbor of a city.

42
00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:02.608
Brick and wooden buildings lined narrow streets.

43
00:03:02.609 --> 00:03:06.352
She could see a white church tower in the distance.

44
00:03:06.353 --> 00:03:10.631
"It looks like we're in a seaport," she said.

45
00:03:10.632 --> 00:03:13.272
"I wonder where?"

46
00:03:13.273 --> 00:03:19.007
Several tall-masted ships were tied to the pier with heavy rope.

47
00:03:19.008 --> 00:03:23.067
One ship was just coming in to dock.

48
00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:30.083
"I can see the ship's name," Mandy said. "The Liberty."

49
00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:31.647
Vinnie pointed.

50
00:03:31.648 --> 00:03:36.410
"It looks like the men over there are waiting for the ship."

51
00:03:36.411 --> 00:03:41.002
Suddenly, the children heard marching feet.

52
00:03:41.003 --> 00:03:43.133
They turned around.

53
00:03:43.134 --> 00:03:49.555
Soldiers wearing red coats and black hats were heading toward the ship in a line.

54
00:03:49.556 --> 00:03:53.293
They held long, thin rifles.

55
00:03:53.294 --> 00:03:57.557
"The Redcoats!" shouted a man on the dock.

56
00:03:57.558 --> 00:04:01.912
Everyone turned to watch the soldiers approach.

57
00:04:01.913 --> 00:04:05.870
"Who are they?" asked Vinnie nervously.

58
00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:08.867
"They look angry."

59
00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:13.823
The Redcoats stopped and held their rifles in front of them.

60
00:04:13.824 --> 00:04:19.009
The leader stepped forward and spoke to one of the men on the dock.

61
00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:24.752
"Vinnie! I think I know where we are!" Mandy almost shouted.

62
00:04:24.753 --> 00:04:29.018
"The Redcoats! Aren't they the British Army?"

63
00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:32.246
Vinnie stared at the soldiers.

64
00:04:32.247 --> 00:04:37.448
"Their uniforms do look familiar . . ." He paused.

65
00:04:37.449 --> 00:04:47.123
"We're still in America!"
